    "summary": "Renders the real provider icon (Claude/Codex/Vibe) in the history and active-chat chrome dropdowns and relabels the empty active-chat placeholder to \"no active work\". Validation-driven fixes: (1) the history menu was left-anchored like the active menu and overflowed the right viewport edge — now right-anchored via #insrc-histmenu{left:auto;right:0}, with the new selector listed in chat-theme's exact-selector assertion; (2) the history-activation subject had no persisted-history-row coverage — added N9 (persisted history row posts open-chat even when absent from the active list). Smoke is a real headless-Chrome run including a viewport-boundary check for the history menu (22 assertions pass, /tmp/insrc-smoke-546198e11c24c1e3-s1.json + .png).",
